kind how-do-i
title How do I set up a private kiosk with two screens, each with its own keyboard?
intro A kiosk of two screens is two paths: each joins one display and one keyboard to a terminal of its own. Under the closed policy, vtium ignores a keyboard that no rule names, so a keyboard plugged in later types into neither terminal.
see heads-and-rules/show-a-terminal-on-a-display

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
device display HDMI-A-1 GSM:0x5b88:LEFT0001
device display DP-1 DEL:0xa0c1:RIGHT0001
device keyboard 046d:c31c Left keyboard
device keyboard 04d9:0169 Right keyboard
device keyboard 1a2c:2124 Visitor keyboard

1. Go to the Flow tab.
2. Highlight HDMI-A-1.
3. Press Space to pick.
4. Highlight Left keyboard.
5. Press Space to pick.
6. Press a to add path.
7. Highlight DP-1.
8. Press Space to pick.
9. Highlight Right keyboard.
10. Press Space to pick.
11. Press a to add path.
12. Press q to quit.
13. Press y to save and quit.
14. Run `vtium-config set policy closed`.
at the policy
check said lacks "error"
check draft display HDMI-A-1 reaches terminal-1
check draft input Left keyboard reaches terminal-1
check draft display DP-1 reaches terminal-2
check draft input Right keyboard reaches terminal-2
check draft input Visitor keyboard reaches ignored
